{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/hwbqtkby","slideIndex":1,"text":"Our dataset contains 1,200 individual reaching trials from two participants. Each participant completed two experimental conditions, with three blocks of 100 trials per condition.\nThe data were collected at 1,000 Hertz, meaning hand movements were recorded every millisecond. This gives us very detailed time-series measurements.\nThe primary variables we examined were hand position, velocity, and acceleration, particularly in the lateral or side-to-side direction.\nOne important preprocessing step was aligning every trial to its recorded Pixel event. We defined this event as time zero and examined movement from 200 milliseconds before to 500 milliseconds after it.\nThis allowed us to compare and average movement trajectories across different trials.\n"}
