{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slideIndex":2,"text":"We also examined how frequently each participant successfully reached the target.\nWe classified trials as hits or misses using the event information recorded in the CSV files.\nOverall, approximately 81% of trials were successful. However, there was a substantial difference between participants.\nParticipant A had a hit rate of 67.5%, compared with 94.3% for Participant B, a difference of approximately 27 percentage points.\nWe also observed some variation across experimental conditions. Participant A performed better in Condition B, while Participant B performed slightly better in Condition A.\nSomething that was interesting was that fast and slow targets had nearly identical overall hit rates.\n"}
